{"Title":"An Act to improve health care workforce development through graduate nursing practice","BillNumber":"H3613","DocketNumber":"HD1444","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"E_C1","Name":"Edward F. Coppinger","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/E_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T12:09:29.7"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"E_C1","Name":"Edward F. Coppinger","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/E_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T12:09:29.7"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3613/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Coppinger of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3613) of Edward F. Coppinger for legislation to improve health care workforce development through graduate nursing practice.  Public Health.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 80 of chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding after the words “five hundred dollars;” the following:-\r\n\t“provided, however, that a student who graduated from a registered nursing program approved by the board of registration in nursing established under section 13 of chapter 13 of the General Laws or who is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a registered nursing program approved by the board may practice nursing, provided, however, that: (i) the individual is employed by or providing health care services at the direction of a licensed health care facility or a licensed health care provider; (ii) the individual is directly supervised while providing health care services; and (iii) the employing licensed health care facility or licensed health care provider has verified that the individual is a graduate of a registered nursing program approved by the board or that the individual is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a registered nursing program approved by the board;”\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 80A of chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding after the words “five hundred dollars;” the following:-\r\n\t“provided, however, a student who graduated from a practical nursing program approved by the board of registration in nursing established under section 13 of chapter 13 of the General Laws or who is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a practical nursing program approved by the board may practice nursing, provided, however, that: (i) the individual is employed by or providing health care services at the direction of a licensed health care facility or a licensed health care provider; (ii) the individual is directly supervised while providing health care services; and (iii) the employing licensed health care facility or licensed health care provider has verified that the individual is a graduate of a practical nursing program approved by the board or that the individual is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a practical nursing program approved by the board.”\r\n\tSECTION 3. Section 80B of chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding at the end thereof the following new paragraph:-\r\n\t“A student who graduated from a registered nursing or practical nursing program approved by the board of registration in nursing established under section 13 of chapter 13 of the General Laws or who is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a registered nursing or practical nursing program approved by the board may practice nursing; provided, however, that: (i) the individual is employed by or providing health care services at the direction of a licensed health care facility or a licensed health care provider; (ii) the individual is directly supervised while providing health care services; and (iii) the employing licensed health care facility or licensed health care provider has verified that the individual is a graduate of a registered nursing or practical nursing program approved by the board or that the individual is a senior nursing student attending the last semester of a registered nursing or practical nursing program approved by the board.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J16","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J16"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J24","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}